{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:74085",
  "title": "Important: nodejs:24 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-01 00:01:35"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-09 00:15:12"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* undici: undici: Authentication bypass via cross-origin cache poisoning due to missing origin isolation (CVE-2026-85152)\n\n* undici: undici: TLS certificate validation bypass in BalancedPool via dropped connect options (CVE-2026-84961)\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol (CVE-2026-19534)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* nodejs:24/nodejs: Rebase to the latest Node.js 24 release [rhel-8.10.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-249188)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
